messages:
nina (design): Quick catch from user testing today — on small phones the Console "Model runs" list gets a horizontal scrollbar. The collapsed sidebar button sits over the row action icons so folks can't tap 'View'. Screenshot: https://imgur.com/console-scroll :frowning:

tom (frontend): repro'd on 360x640. Looks like the actions column is min-width'd so it forces table width.

vicky (product): this blocks quick triage flows on mobile. Users expected to open run details from list view.

leo (mobile): two ideas: 1) hide secondary actions behind kebab at <=400px, 2) convert the sidebar to an overlay that slides over content (not push). Overlay can be dismissed with swipe or close icon.

nina (design): prefer overlay — keeps list stable. Also propose stacking label/value pairs in each row under 420px so the main identifier is always left-aligned and actions sit below. I'll mock 320/375/414 variants.

tom (frontend): stacking is doable. Concern: we use react-window for virtualization. If we change row DOM to include hidden expanded blocks, virtualization still fine as long as row height is predictable or we use dynamic sizing via VariableSizeList.

maya (qa): note for QA: also check landscape on small devices — when orientation changes the overlay should remain full-height and not create a second scrollbar.

aria-a11y-bot: a11y reminders: overlay must have role="dialog" and aria-modal="true", restore focus to the triggering action, and ensure keyboard dismiss (Esc) is available. Kebab menu must be accessible via logical reading order when rows stack.

vicky (product): copy tweak: kebab menu label should be "More actions" for screen reader. Drawer header should show short run id then secondary line with full model name (ellipsis + detailed on long press).

tom (frontend): plan: 1) add CSS breakpoint @media (max-width: 420px) to switch table -> stacked row layout, 2) actions move into kebab with a visually-hidden label "More actions"; 3) sidebar becomes modal overlay on small widths with slide-in animation. Will prototype with Feature Flag ff_mobile_table_layout.

leo (mobile): when implementing overlay, use fixed positioning with safe-area-inset padding for iOS notch. Also ensure swipe-to-close doesn't conflict with horizontal carousels in other screens.

nina (design): uploaded mocks: https://figma.com/file/abcdef/mobile-table-overview — includes stacked rows, kebab layout, overlay states. QA checklist in figma notes.

maya (qa): added manual test cases to ticket: touch target sizes for kebab, no horizontal scroll at 320/375/412 widths, overlay focus trap, landscape behavior.

tom (frontend): I'll open spike PR today. I'll include CSS snippet in PR description: ```css
@media (max-width:420px) {
  .runs-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .runs-actions {
    order: 2;
    align-self: flex-end;
  }
  .runs-kebab { display:block; }
}
```

nina (design): small visual tweak: ensure identifier font-weight is 600 on mobile for scannability, secondary lines 12px/regular.

vicky (product): timeline: can we include in the 2.3.1 patch? Mobile UX regression is high priority.

tom (frontend): aiming for PR by Wed, QA Thu, merge Fri if no blockers. Will toggle ff_mobile_table_layout for canary first.

aria-a11y-bot: checklist reminder: announce state changes to screen readers when overlay opens (aria-live if necessary).

nina (design): thanks everyone. I'll add acceptance criteria to ticket: no horizontal scroll @320/375/412, kebab accessible and sized 44px min, overlay has focus trap and restores focus, long model names truncated with long-press to show full string. :thumbsup:
